Apple has confirmed the battery capacities for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/apple-announces-iphone-18-pro-and-iphone-18-pro-max/">iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max</a> models that the company announced earlier today.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iPhone-18-Pro-Battery.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063582" /><br/>
Apple is required to publish energy labels on its <a href="https://www.apple.com/ie/shop/buy-iphone/iphone-18-pro">iPhone product pages in the EU</a>, and they reveal the official mAh battery capacities for the devices.<br/>
<br/>
Here are the battery capacities for the iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max models that still have a SIM card tray, according to Apple:<br/>
<br/>
<ul><br/>
  <li><strong>iPhone 18 Pro:</strong> 4,056 mAh (+1.7% vs. iPhone 17 Pro's 3,988 mAh)</li><br/>
  <li><strong>iPhone 18 Pro Max:</strong> 5,391 mAh (+11.7% vs. iPhone 17 Pro Max's 4,823 mAh)</li><br/>
</ul>Notably, the iPhone 18 Pro Max has received a much larger battery life increase than the iPhone 18 Pro did compared to the previous generation.<br/>
<br/>
eSIM-only models of the iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max will be available in Bahrain, Canada, Guam, Japan, Kuwait, Mexico, Oman, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, the U.S., and the U.S. Virgin Islands. The devices have a SIM card tray in all other countries around the world, including in the U.K. and the rest of Europe.<br/>
<br/>
eSIM-only iPhone models are equipped with a slightly larger battery that fills the space occupied by the physical SIM card tray.<br/>
<br/>
